cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'ReaLLM: Transparent Intelligence'
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hassan Nejad
    given-names: Mohsen
    email: mohsen.nejad94@gmail.com
    affiliation: 'Tallinn University, Lusófona University, and Tampere University - AI for Sustainable Societies (AISS) Program'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/TechNejad/ReaLLM'
url: 'https://reallm.netlify.app/'
abstract: >-
  ReaLLM is a research prototype that reveals what typical AI chatbots
  hide: the system prompts and constraints that guide every response.
  This project explores interface-level transparency as a safety mechanism,
  making AI constraints visible and understandable to everyone, not just
  AI researchers.
keywords:
  - AI transparency
  - AI safety
  - system prompts
  - human-AI interaction
  - explainable AI
  - research prototype
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2025-01-28'
